title: Eventos del foco
max-visits: 1
view-if: 0
# Container/namespace only — NOT tagged event. banda="sierra", f_phase="marcha".
#
# EVERY event in this file is a CHAIN: a first decision opens a second, and the conclusion is
# computed from both of them together with the state of the water (apoyo_popular), the record
# (brutalidad), and the enemy. Carriers between stages: ch_p1 / ch_p2 (what you chose),
# ch_n1 / ch_n2 (hidden numbers the player never sees), ch_res (which ending fired).
# The point of view is the guerrilla's: you see what a person in the column would see, and you
# find out what it cost afterwards, the way they did.

# =====================================================================
# LA COSECHA — the harvest is given. Then it has to be moved. Then the army goes looking for it.
# =====================================================================
@ev_cosecha
title: La cosecha
new-page: true
face-image: img/cards/ejido.jpg
subtitle: Forty sacks, given freely — and eleven kilometres of open trail
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and apoyo_popular >= 35 and time >= f_ev_last + 2
priority: 3
frequency: 60
max-visits: 8
on-arrival: {! Q.f_ev_last=Q.time; Q.ch_p1=""; Q.ch_p2=""; Q.ch_res=""; !}

= La cosecha

They do not announce it. You come down into the valley at dusk and the sacks are already stacked under the ramada by the church — coffee, maize, a little dried meat, forty sacks that nobody will admit to having put there. Half the valley is standing around not looking at them. An old woman finally says, to nobody, that the harvest was good this year and that some of it seems to have been left out in the weather.

This is the line between a guerrilla and a bandit, and it is not a line you draw. They draw it. The bandit takes and the valley informs; the rooted column is *given*, and the whole valley covers for it afterwards. What you do in the next ten seconds, in front of everyone, is the answer to a question they have been asking about you for two years.

- @cos_recibir: Take it as what it is — a gift between people on the same side. Say thank you and mean it. *(the column eats; the giving is confirmed)*
- @cos_pagar: Put money on the table anyway, though they will push it back. *(costs the little you have; nobody can ever say the guerrilla ate the poor)*
- @cos_mitad: Take half. Tell them to put the rest back in their own granaries where it belongs. *(less food; something else entirely)*

# ---- stage 2: the transport problem ----
@cos_recibir
new-page: true
go-to: foco_eventos.cos_mover
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p1="recibir"; Q.f_comida+=14; Q.f_parque+=3; Q.apoyo_popular+=2; !}

@cos_pagar
new-page: true
go-to: foco_eventos.cos_mover
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p1="pagar"; Q.f_comida+=10; Q.funds=(Q.funds||0)-3; if(Q.funds<0){Q.funds=0;} Q.apoyo_popular+=5; Q.sup_peasants=(Q.sup_peasants||0)+2; !}

@cos_mitad
new-page: true
go-to: foco_eventos.cos_mover
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p1="mitad"; Q.f_comida+=6; Q.apoyo_popular+=7; Q.sup_peasants=(Q.sup_peasants||0)+3; Q.f_moral+=3; !}

@cos_mover
title: Cómo se sube
new-page: true
face-image: img/camino.jpg
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_n1=0; !}

= Cómo se sube

[? if ch_p1 = "recibir" : You take it, and the taking is easy and correct and nobody in the plaza says anything about it, which is its own kind of approval. ?][? if ch_p1 = "pagar" : You put the money down on a sack and the old woman looks at it like it is an insult, and then like it is not, and then she looks away. The coins stay on the sack. Somebody will tell that story in four villages by Sunday. ?][? if ch_p1 = "mitad" : You take twenty sacks and tell them to carry the rest back up to their own lofts, and there is an argument about it — they are offended, actually offended, that you would think them unable to feed you. You lose the argument gracefully and take twenty sacks anyway. ?]

And then you are standing in a plaza at nightfall with several hundred kilos of food and a camp eleven kilometres away, up a trail that crosses open ground twice, in a district where a spotter plane goes over most mornings. Grain is the easiest thing in the world to follow. It leaves a track, it leaves a smell, it leaves a hole in a granary that a lieutenant with a clipboard can measure.

- @cos_m_mulas: Night mule train, the high trail, three trips. *(slow — three nights of exposure — but nothing crosses the open ground in daylight)*
- @cos_m_casas: Split it among twenty houses and collect it a kilo at a time over a month. *(invisible; but now twenty families are holding guerrilla supplies)*
- @cos_m_columna: One lift, tonight, the whole column carrying and covering. *(fast and heavy and very visible)*

@cos_m_mulas
go-to: foco_eventos.cos_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="mulas"; Q.ch_n1=8; Q.f_cerco+=5; !}

@cos_m_casas
go-to: foco_eventos.cos_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="casas"; Q.ch_n1=-6; Q.f_comida-=3; !}

@cos_m_columna
go-to: foco_eventos.cos_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="columna"; Q.ch_n1=18; Q.f_cerco+=12; if(Q.f_cerco>100){Q.f_cerco=100;} !}

# ---- stage 3: the lieutenant with the clipboard ----
@cos_fin
new-page: true
face-image: img/countryside2.jpg
on-arrival: {!
var _lealtad=(Q.apoyo_popular||0)-(Q.brutalidad||0)*4+((Q.ch_p1==="pagar")?14:0)+((Q.ch_p1==="mitad")?20:0)+((Q.zona_gobernada===1)?8:0);
var _riesgo=(Q.ch_n1||0)+(Q.estado_intel||0)*0.35+(Q.f_cerco||0)*0.12-((Q.apoyo_popular||0)*0.18)+(Math.random()*22-11);
Q.ch_res="limpio";
if(_riesgo>=16){ Q.ch_res=(_lealtad>=40)?"visita":"quemado"; }
else if(_riesgo>=6){ Q.ch_res=(_lealtad>=30)?"limpio":"visita"; }
if(Q.ch_res==="visita"){ Q.f_cerco+=8; Q.estado_intel=(Q.estado_intel||0)+3; Q.apoyo_popular-=2; }
if(Q.ch_res==="quemado"){ Q.f_comida-=10; Q.apoyo_popular-=9; Q.memorial=(Q.memorial||0)+2; Q.f_cerco+=16; Q.estado_intel=(Q.estado_intel||0)+8; Q.represion=(Q.represion||0)+2; Q.f_moral-=6; }
if(Q.ch_res==="limpio" && Q.ch_p1!=="recibir"){ var _h=Math.max(0,(Q.apoyo_techo||55)-(Q.apoyo_popular||0)); Q.apoyo_popular+=Math.min(5,_h*0.3); }
if(Q.f_comida<0){Q.f_comida=0;} if(Q.apoyo_popular<0){Q.apoyo_popular=0;} if(Q.f_cerco>100){Q.f_cerco=100;} if(Q.f_moral<0){Q.f_moral=0;}
!}

= El teniente y la libreta

[? if ch_res = "limpio" : The food is in the caches inside the month and nothing follows it. That sentence is doing a great deal of quiet work: somewhere in it are a boy who told a patrol the wrong thing about mules, a granary book with a page torn out, and an entire valley agreeing without meeting about what it did not see. Nobody will ever tell you about any of that. You will simply notice, over the years, that when you are careful with these people the arithmetic keeps coming out in your favour, and that when you are not, it does not. ?][? if ch_res = "visita" : A lieutenant comes up to the village with a clipboard and a theory about the difference between last year's harvest and this one, and he spends a day being lied to with enormous politeness by people who have decided, on balance, to lie. He leaves with nothing except the certainty that he was lied to, which he writes down. The food is safe. The file thickens. That is the trade, and this time you got the better half of it. ?][? if ch_res = "quemado" : They find it. [? if ch_p2 = "casas" : Twenty houses were holding it, which means twenty houses to search, and the soldiers only had to be right once. ?][? if ch_p2 = "columna" : Somebody counted the column going up the trail under load, in the dark, and counted it going down empty, and drew the obvious line between the two. ?][? if ch_p2 = "mulas" : Three nights was two nights too many. ?] They burn what they find in the yard where they find it and take two men to Atoyac to explain it, and the valley stands in the smoke doing arithmetic of its own — *we gave them the harvest and this is what the harvest bought us.* You cannot argue with that arithmetic. You can only try to be the sort of movement it comes out differently for next year. ?]

- @root: Continuar.

# =====================================================================
# LOS QUE QUIEREN ENTRAR — recruitment, then one specific boy, then what he becomes.
# =====================================================================
@ev_reclutas
title: Los que quieren entrar
new-page: true
face-image: img/adelitas.jpg
subtitle: Everyone who comes up the mountain is somebody's whole family
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and apoyo_popular >= 40 and f_hombres < 45 and time >= f_ev_last + 2
priority: 3
frequency: 55
max-visits: 8
on-arrival: {! Q.f_ev_last=Q.time; Q.ch_p1=""; Q.ch_p2=""; Q.ch_res=""; !}

= Los que quieren entrar

They come up in twos and threes and they wait at the edge of the camp until somebody notices them, which is a thing that takes a particular kind of courage. A boy whose brother went to the airbase and did not come back. A girl who can already outshoot half the column and knows it and is trying very hard not to show that she knows it. A campesino of maybe fifty who has worked out that a machete against a G-3 is still better than kneeling, and who says so without any drama at all, which is how you know he means it.

Recruits are the only reinforcement a foco ever gets. They are also mouths, and risk, and the problem Che named in the diary and never solved: a band that grows faster than it can train or feed is a band that dies of its own weight, in the field, on a bad afternoon, because somebody green did the wrong thing at the wrong moment.

- @rec_todos: Take them all. The villages are offering their children and refusing that offer has a cost too. *(numbers now; thin food, green hands)*
- @rec_vetar: Take only who the base will vouch for by blood, and train them properly before they carry anything. *(fewer, steadier)*
- @rec_devolver: Turn them all back with a task: organize your own village, wait, we will come for you. *(no growth; a bench in every hamlet)*

@rec_todos
new-page: true
go-to: foco_eventos.rec_chamaco
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p1="todos"; Q.f_hombres+=7; Q.f_comida-=7; Q.f_moral-=2; Q.apoyo_popular+=2; Q.f_reclutas=(Q.f_reclutas||0)+7; Q.disciplina=(Q.disciplina||65)-3; !}

@rec_vetar
new-page: true
go-to: foco_eventos.rec_chamaco
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p1="vetar"; Q.f_hombres+=3; Q.disciplina=(Q.disciplina||65)+5; Q.f_moral+=2; Q.f_reclutas=(Q.f_reclutas||0)+3; !}

@rec_devolver
new-page: true
go-to: foco_eventos.rec_chamaco
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p1="devolver"; Q.disciplina=(Q.disciplina||65)+2; Q.sup_peasants=(Q.sup_peasants||0)+3; Q.apoyo_popular+=3; !}

@rec_chamaco
title: El chamaco
new-page: true
face-image: img/cards/recluta.jpg

= El chamaco

There is one left over after the decision is made, and he is the problem. He is fourteen — he says sixteen, and he has practised saying it. His brother was taken off a bus at the Atoyac checkpoint eight months ago and the family has been to the barracks eleven times. He has no other plan. He is not going home; if you send him down the mountain he will simply come back up it, or go and find somebody less careful than you to give him a rifle.

He is also small enough and unremarkable enough that he could walk through any checkpoint in the state carrying anything at all, and nobody would look at him twice.

- @rec_c_fusil: Give him a rifle and put him in a squad with a veteran who will keep him alive. *(a fighter; he is fourteen)*
- @rec_c_correo: No rifle. Make him a courier — the one thing he is uniquely good at, and the one job where being fourteen is an advantage. *(useful and safer; you are still using a child)*
- @rec_c_escuela: Send him to the village school in the zone and tell him the movement needs him literate more than armed. *(he will hate you; it may be the only clean thing you do this year)*

@rec_c_fusil
go-to: foco_eventos.rec_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="fusil"; Q.f_hombres+=1; Q.f_reclutas=(Q.f_reclutas||0)+1; !}

@rec_c_correo
go-to: foco_eventos.rec_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="correo"; Q.inteligencia=(Q.inteligencia||0)+3; !}

@rec_c_escuela
go-to: foco_eventos.rec_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="escuela"; Q.apoyo_popular+=3; Q.zona_gobernada=1; !}

@rec_fin
new-page: true
face-image: img/guerillasmile.jpg
on-arrival: {!
var _form=(Q.disciplina||65)+((Q.ch_p1==="vetar")?18:0)+((Q.ch_p1==="devolver")?12:0)-((Q.ch_p1==="todos")?12:0)+(Q.f_moral||0)*0.25;
var _roll=_form-70+(Math.random()*40-18);
Q.ch_res="bien";
if(Q.ch_p2==="fusil"){ if(_roll>=8){Q.ch_res="fusil_bien";} else if(_roll>=-10){Q.ch_res="fusil_gris";} else {Q.ch_res="fusil_mal";} }
else if(Q.ch_p2==="correo"){ if(_roll>=-4){Q.ch_res="correo_bien";} else {Q.ch_res="correo_mal";} }
else { Q.ch_res="escuela_fin"; }
if(Q.ch_res==="fusil_bien"){ Q.f_moral+=6; Q.leyenda=(Q.leyenda||0)+2; Q.inteligencia=(Q.inteligencia||0)+3; }
if(Q.ch_res==="fusil_gris"){ Q.f_moral-=3; }
if(Q.ch_res==="fusil_mal"){ Q.f_hombres-=2; Q.f_bajas=(Q.f_bajas||0)+2; Q.memorial=(Q.memorial||0)+3; Q.f_moral-=10; Q.apoyo_popular-=6; }
if(Q.ch_res==="correo_bien"){ Q.inteligencia=(Q.inteligencia||0)+5; Q.f_cerco-=6; if(Q.f_cerco<0){Q.f_cerco=0;} }
if(Q.ch_res==="correo_mal"){ Q.estado_intel=(Q.estado_intel||0)+10; Q.f_cerco+=14; Q.memorial=(Q.memorial||0)+2; Q.apoyo_popular-=5; Q.f_moral-=8; }
if(Q.ch_res==="escuela_fin"){ Q.sup_peasants=(Q.sup_peasants||0)+2; Q.f_moral+=2; }
if(Q.f_cerco>100){Q.f_cerco=100;} if(Q.apoyo_popular<0){Q.apoyo_popular=0;} if(Q.f_moral<0){Q.f_moral=0;} if(Q.f_hombres<0){Q.f_hombres=0;}
if(Q.f_hombres<=0){Q.f_fin_foco=1;Q.members=0;}
!}

= Lo que pasó con él

[? if ch_res = "fusil_bien" : He turns out to be one of those people the sierra occasionally produces who is simply better at this than the adults are. He is silent on a march, he does not fire when he is told not to fire, and within a year he is reading ground for the whole column and correcting veterans about it, politely, and being right. Nobody calls him the chamaco any more. You will think about this the next time somebody tells you the column has to stop taking children, and you will not have a good answer, because he is the argument for it and he is also fourteen. ?][? if ch_res = "fusil_gris" : He is neither good nor bad; he is a boy carrying a rifle that is too big for him and doing his best in a war that has no use for anyone's best. He fires early once and gets shouted at, and cries about it out of sight of the camp, and does not do it again. He survives the season. That is all you get to say about most people up here. ?][? if ch_res = "fusil_mal" : It happens on an ordinary afternoon, in the way it always happens: the column is crossing open ground, something moves, and somebody green fires at it, and then everyone is firing and then the army knows where you are. He is one of the two you leave up there. His mother comes to the camp four days later and does not shout at you, which is far worse, and asks only for the body and where exactly it happened. The column takes children because the villages offer them. This is the invoice for that policy and it arrives, eventually, every time. ?][? if ch_res = "correo_bien" : He walks through checkpoints twice a week with things sewn into the lining of a jacket and soldiers ruffle his hair. He learns the whole road network of the district the way other boys learn a football league. He is worth more than a squad and he is in less danger than anyone in the column, and the small dishonest thing you never say out loud is that this is *also* using a fourteen-year-old, just in a way that lets you sleep. ?][? if ch_res = "correo_mal" : They pick him up at the Atoyac checkpoint on a Tuesday with a message in his shoe, and he is fourteen, and they have all afternoon. Nobody in the column blames him for what comes out; a grown man with training would have talked too. What you cannot get past is that you chose him for the job precisely because soldiers do not look hard at boys, and it turns out they look hard at boys once they have a reason to. The safest job in the column was safe until it was not, and it was never his risk to weigh. ?][? if ch_res = "escuela_fin" : He does not speak to you for two months. He sits in the school in the zone, furious, being the oldest and angriest person in a room of eight-year-olds, learning to read properly. Then one afternoon he is helping the teacher with the little ones, still angry, still good at it. He may hate you for years. Somewhere under the anger is the fact that you are the first adult in his life who wanted something for him rather than from him — and one of the few decisions of this war that will still look right in thirty years. ?]

- @root: Continuar.

# =====================================================================
# EL AJUSTICIAMIENTO — the accusation, the evidence, the sentence.
# =====================================================================
@ev_ajusticiamiento
title: El ajusticiamiento
new-page: true
face-image: img/guardias_blancas.jpg
subtitle: A name, a rope, and no way to be certain
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and f_cerco >= 40 and time >= f_ev_last + 3
priority: 4
frequency: 45
max-visits: 5
on-arrival: {! Q.f_ev_last=Q.time; Q.ch_p1=""; Q.ch_p2=""; Q.ch_res=""; Q.ch_n1=(Math.random()<0.62)?1:0; !}

= El ajusticiamiento

They bring you a name and a rope in the same conversation, which tells you what has already been decided by everyone except you.

The man is from the valley. He has a store, or he had a nephew in the judicial police, or he was seen twice on the road to the barracks in a month when things went wrong twice. The Partido de los Pobres kept a whole brigade for exactly this — the Brigada Campesina de *Ajusticiamiento*, the peasant brigade whose middle name was the killing of the ones the villages could not bear any longer. It is not an accident that the brigade was named for the killing rather than the fighting. Fear is real, and a dead informer informs no more.

And you have been in this war long enough to know the other thing: that half the informers who ever got shot in a clearing at dawn were not informers, and that the column which learns to kill on a suspicion has taught itself an arithmetic it will one day apply inward.

- @aju_ahora: Do it tonight. The village asked, the column's security demands it, and hesitation is how commanders get people killed. *(fast; you will never know)*
- @aju_probar: Stop. Nobody dies on a feeling — find out what is actually true first. *(costs time and standing; the truth is not always a relief)*
- @aju_asamblea: Take it to the assembly. Let the village that accused him judge him in daylight, with witnesses, and own the result. *(slow; makes the movement into a kind of law)*

# ---- branch A: no evidence, straight to it ----
@aju_ahora
new-page: true
go-to: foco_eventos.aju_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p1="ahora"; Q.ch_p2="ninguna"; !}

# ---- branch B: the evidence ----
@aju_probar
new-page: true
face-image: img/charola.jpg
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p1="probar"; Q.f_cerco+=6; if(Q.f_cerco>100){Q.f_cerco=100;} !}

= Lo que se averigua

It takes nine days and two people you could not spare, and the column mutters the entire time about a commander who protects suspects.

[? if ch_n1 = 1 : What comes back is not ambiguous. He was paid — not much, a sum that would embarrass a serious man — and he was paid three times, and the last payment lines up to the day with the patrol that killed Refugio on the Río Santiago. There is also this, which nobody wanted: they had his daughter for two days in November before the first payment. He did not volunteer. He broke. Those are different things everywhere in the world except in a war, where they produce the same corpse. ?][? if ch_n1 = 0 : What comes back is nothing. The road to the barracks goes past his sister's house and always has. The two bad months were bad for four other columns in the state as well. The man who accused him owes him money over a boundary dispute that started in 1961. There is no informer here. There is a frightened village that needed the losses to have a face, and a face was available. ?]

Now you have to do something with a truth that has made the decision harder rather than easier.

- @aju_p_igual: [? if ch_n1 = 1 : He broke and men died. Carry it out. ?][? if ch_n1 = 0 : The suspicion is out in the open now and it will not go back in the bottle. Carry it out anyway. ?]
- @aju_p_exilio: Exile him. Out of the district by morning, his family with him, and the whole valley told exactly why. *(no body; no certainty either)*
- @aju_p_perdon: Let him stay, marked and watched, and say publicly what was done to him and by whom. *(the risk walks around on two legs)*

@aju_p_igual
go-to: foco_eventos.aju_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="igual"; !}

@aju_p_exilio
go-to: foco_eventos.aju_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="exilio"; !}

@aju_p_perdon
go-to: foco_eventos.aju_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="perdon"; !}

# ---- branch C: the assembly ----
@aju_asamblea
new-page: true
face-image: img/elpueblo.jpg
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p1="asamblea"; Q.zona_gobernada=1; !}

= La asamblea

It takes a whole day and it is the strangest thing the column has ever organized: two hundred people in the churchyard, the accused sitting on a chair rather than kneeling, witnesses called in order, and the guerrilla standing at the back with its rifles pointedly grounded because the entire meaning of the exercise is that the guns are not deciding this.

It is also excruciating. People say true things and untrue things at equal volume. An old man gives forty minutes of evidence about a fence.

[? if ch_n1 = 1 : By the afternoon it is clear even to his own cousins that he took money, and clear too that they took his daughter first, and the churchyard goes very quiet when that part comes out. Then the assembly has to decide, and it is theirs to decide, which is the entire point and is also the moment you understand what you have handed them. ?][? if ch_n1 = 0 : By the afternoon the case has collapsed in public, which is the best thing that could have happened and does not feel like it, because a man has spent a day being tried in front of his neighbours for nothing, and the neighbour who accused him is sitting four metres away, and both of them still have to live here. ?]

- @aju_a_acatar: Whatever they decide, the movement carries it out. You do not get to hand people a court and then overrule it. *(the sierra gets law; law is not always mercy)*
- @aju_a_clemencia: Ask them, as a compañero rather than a commander, for clemency — and take the political hit if they resent it. *(you spend your standing to keep a man alive)*

@aju_a_acatar
go-to: foco_eventos.aju_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="acatar"; !}

@aju_a_clemencia
go-to: foco_eventos.aju_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="clemencia"; !}

@aju_fin
new-page: true
face-image: img/muertos.jpg
on-arrival: {!
var _p1=Q.ch_p1||"", _p2=Q.ch_p2||"", _cul=Q.ch_n1||0;
Q.ch_res="";
if(_p1==="ahora"){ Q.ch_res=(_cul===1)?"ahora_bien":"ahora_mal"; }
else if(_p1==="probar"){
  if(_p2==="igual"){ Q.ch_res=(_cul===1)?"just_culpable":"just_inocente"; }
  else if(_p2==="exilio"){ Q.ch_res="exilio"; }
  else { Q.ch_res="perdon"; }
} else {
  if(_p2==="acatar"){ Q.ch_res=(_cul===1)?"asam_sentencia":"asam_absuelto"; }
  else { Q.ch_res="asam_clemencia"; }
}
var R=Q.ch_res;
if(R==="ahora_bien"){ Q.brutalidad=(Q.brutalidad||0)+2; Q.ajusticiamientos=(Q.ajusticiamientos||0)+1; Q.f_cerco-=10; Q.apoyo_popular-=3; Q.paranoia=(Q.paranoia||8)+5; }
if(R==="ahora_mal"){ Q.brutalidad=(Q.brutalidad||0)+3; Q.ajusticiamientos=(Q.ajusticiamientos||0)+1; Q.apoyo_popular-=11; Q.paranoia=(Q.paranoia||8)+12; Q.f_moral-=8; Q.disciplina=(Q.disciplina||65)-6; Q.estado_intel=(Q.estado_intel||0)+4; }
if(R==="just_culpable"){ Q.brutalidad=(Q.brutalidad||0)+1; Q.ajusticiamientos=(Q.ajusticiamientos||0)+1; Q.f_cerco-=12; Q.apoyo_popular-=2; Q.disciplina=(Q.disciplina||65)+2; }
if(R==="just_inocente"){ Q.brutalidad=(Q.brutalidad||0)+4; Q.ajusticiamientos=(Q.ajusticiamientos||0)+1; Q.apoyo_popular-=14; Q.paranoia=(Q.paranoia||8)+16; Q.f_moral-=12; Q.disciplina=(Q.disciplina||65)-10; }
if(R==="exilio"){ Q.f_cerco-=4; Q.apoyo_popular+=2; Q.estado_intel=(Q.estado_intel||0)+3; }
if(R==="perdon"){ Q.f_cerco+=8; var _h=Math.max(0,(Q.apoyo_techo||55)-(Q.apoyo_popular||0)); Q.apoyo_popular+=Math.min(6,_h*0.35); Q.f_moral+=3; Q.leyenda=(Q.leyenda||0)+1; }
if(R==="asam_sentencia"){ Q.ajusticiamientos=(Q.ajusticiamientos||0)+1; Q.brutalidad=(Q.brutalidad||0)+1; Q.f_cerco-=10; var _h2=Math.max(0,(Q.apoyo_techo||55)-(Q.apoyo_popular||0)); Q.apoyo_popular+=Math.min(7,_h2*0.4); Q.sup_peasants=(Q.sup_peasants||0)+3; }
if(R==="asam_absuelto"){ var _h3=Math.max(0,(Q.apoyo_techo||55)-(Q.apoyo_popular||0)); Q.apoyo_popular+=Math.min(9,_h3*0.5); Q.paranoia=(Q.paranoia||8)-10; Q.sup_peasants=(Q.sup_peasants||0)+3; Q.f_cerco+=5; }
if(R==="asam_clemencia"){ Q.apoyo_popular-=3; Q.f_moral+=4; Q.leyenda=(Q.leyenda||0)+2; Q.f_cerco+=6; }
if(Q.paranoia<0){Q.paranoia=0;} if(Q.f_cerco<0){Q.f_cerco=0;} if(Q.f_cerco>100){Q.f_cerco=100;} if(Q.apoyo_popular<0){Q.apoyo_popular=0;} if(Q.f_moral<0){Q.f_moral=0;}
!}

= Después

[? if ch_res = "ahora_bien" : It is done before dawn at the edge of the maize, and you find out afterwards — from the payments, from a talkative cousin, from the fact that the leaks stop — that he was in fact the man. You were right. You want that to feel like something and it does not, particularly, because you were right the way a man is right who guesses a number: you did not know it when you gave the order. Neither did anybody else. What the column learned tonight is not that you have good judgement. It is that a name is enough. ?][? if ch_res = "ahora_mal" : It is done before dawn at the edge of the maize. Six weeks later the leak happens again, twice, in a district where the only suspect is buried. Nobody says anything to you about it. Everybody has worked it out. His widow still sells at the Sunday market and she does not look at the column when it passes and the column does not look at her, and the valley has learned that the guerrilla will kill a man on the word of a neighbour who owed him money. The army could not have bought that. You gave it to them for free. ?][? if ch_res = "just_culpable" : You knew before you did it, which is more than most commanders in this war can say, and it makes it worse rather than better: you knew about the payments and you also knew about the two days in November and about the daughter, and you did it anyway, because a column cannot survive a man who breaks and there is no mechanism in a guerrilla war for a person who is guilty and not to blame. The column respects the way you handled it. You will think about the daughter for a long time. ?][? if ch_res = "just_inocente" : You spent nine days proving he was innocent and then killed him because the accusation could not be put back in the bottle. There is no version of the story you can tell that survives contact with that sentence. It gets around — these things always get around, the sierra is a very small place — and the water in this district changes character permanently. People still help you. They help you the way you help a dangerous animal you cannot get rid of. Everything the movement said about itself is now a thing it says. ?][? if ch_res = "exilio" : They are gone by morning: a truck, a sister in Michoacán, and the whole valley told plainly what he did and what was done to him first. It satisfies nobody. The hard men think you are soft, the family thinks you are cruel, and a man who knows where three of your caches are is now living somewhere you cannot see him. It is the option that requires you to tolerate an unresolved risk indefinitely, which is a specific kind of courage nobody writes corridos about. ?][? if ch_res = "perdon" : He stays, marked, watched, working his own land under the eyes of a village that now knows exactly what he did — which is a heavier sentence than the rope in a place this small. Some of the column will never forgive you. But you did not climb up this mountain to become the thing in the palace, and a movement that kills its way to safety has already lost the argument it came here to make. The water runs cleaner for it. The ring runs tighter. Both bills are real and you chose which to pay. ?][? if ch_res = "asam_sentencia" : The assembly hears it all and sentences him itself, and it is the village that carries it out, and the guerrilla stands at the back with its rifles grounded exactly as it promised. It is not merciful. Communities are rarely merciful about this. But something happened in that churchyard that has not happened in the sierra in living memory: a decision of life and death was made in public, by the people it concerned, with evidence, and everybody had to look at it. That is the thing the state has never once offered these valleys. You will lose sleep over it. You will not lose the district. ?][? if ch_res = "asam_absuelto" : The assembly hears it all and acquits him, in the open, with the accuser sitting right there, and then everybody has to go home to the same twelve streets. It is awkward and enormous. The fever that had been building in the valley for four months breaks that afternoon, and the column — which had been three weeks from hunting a ghost through its own ranks — exhales without quite understanding why. The most important thing the guerrilla did this year was hold a meeting and lose control of the outcome. ?][? if ch_res = "asam_clemencia" : You ask them, as a compañero and not as the man with the rifles, to let him live, and they do it — resentfully, conditionally, and because you asked. It works. It also spends something: they gave you a verdict and you leaned on it, and now everyone in the churchyard understands that the assembly decides right up until the guerrilla would rather it did not. You saved a life with the one currency you cannot mint more of. ?]

- @root: Continuar.

# =====================================================================
# LA REPRESALIA — they burn a village for you. Then there are survivors.
# =====================================================================
@ev_represalia
title: La represalia
new-page: true
face-image: img/anti-guerillas2.jpg
subtitle: They cannot find you, so they punish the ones who hide you
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and f_cerco >= 45 and time >= f_reprisal_last + 4
priority: 6
frequency: 50
max-visits: 5
on-arrival: {! Q.f_reprisal_last=Q.time; Q.ch_p1=""; Q.ch_p2=""; Q.ch_res=""; !}

= La represalia

You hear it before you see it, which is how you hear most things up here: two days of nothing from a valley that sends somebody up every week, and then smoke on the wrong side of the ridge in the wrong season for burning.

El Quemado, or a village exactly like it. Emptied at gunpoint because a lieutenant was certain it fed you. He was right; it did. The men have gone to the airbase with the runway pointing at the sea. The granaries are ash and the animals are shot in the corrals and there are eleven houses with the roofs pulled in.

This is the dirty war's logic and it is also, if you can bear to look at it clearly while standing in it, the war's central mistake: every village burned for you sends its survivors up the mountain looking for the people they were burned for loving. That sentence is true. It is also an obscene thing to be thinking while a woman is telling you what happened to her house.

- @rep_vengar: Answer it. Break the garrison that did it, publicly, so the sierra sees that touching the people has a price. *(escalation; the sierra watches)*
- @rep_alejar: Take the column out of the district. You are the weather that came here; leave, and it goes with you. *(saves them; feels like abandonment because it partly is)*
- @rep_defender: Move the column *toward* them and stand between the village and the next sweep. *(the thing a people's army is for, and the thing that gets people's armies killed)*

@rep_vengar
new-page: true
go-to: foco_eventos.rep_sobrevivientes
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p1="vengar"; Q.f_desgaste+=8; Q.leyenda=(Q.leyenda||0)+3; Q.legitimidad_regimen-=3; Q.f_parque-=6; if(Q.f_parque<0){Q.f_parque=0;} Q.f_cerco+=12; if(Q.f_cerco>100){Q.f_cerco=100;} Q.represion=(Q.represion||0)+3; !}

