@rep_sobrevivientes
title: Los que quedan
new-page: true
face-image: img/elpueblo.jpg

= Los que quedan

[? if ch_p1 = "vengar" : You broke a garrison column on the road out of Atoyac and the whole state heard about it inside a week. ?][? if ch_p1 = "alejar" : You took the column three valleys north and the sweeps followed you, exactly as you said they would. ?][? if ch_p1 = "defender" : You put the column between the village and the second sweep, and the second sweep did not get down into the houses. ?]

And now, after the decision that felt like the decision, there is the part nobody writes corridos about: fifty-odd people are sitting on a hillside with what they could carry. Mostly women, all the children, four old men. No maize, no roofs, no men of working age, and the rains in six weeks. They are looking at you because you are the only institution in this valley that has ever done anything, which is a terrible thing to be.

- @rep_s_incorporar: Bring them into the column's zone — feed them from your stores, put them under your protection, make them yours. *(a heavy weight on thin supply; the deepest bond there is)*
- @rep_s_reubicar: Move them to the villages three valleys over that will take them in, and get them out of the war. *(they live; the valley empties; your base empties with it)*
- @rep_s_reconstruir: Rebuild. The whole column on roofs and granaries for a month instead of on operations. *(a month of no war; a village that exists because of you)*
- @rep_s_testigo: Get them and their testimony to the outside — the Church, the press, the exiles, anyone who will write it down. *(no material help at all; the world hears El Quemado's name)*

@rep_s_incorporar
go-to: foco_eventos.rep_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="incorporar"; !}

@rep_s_reubicar
go-to: foco_eventos.rep_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="reubicar"; !}

@rep_s_reconstruir
go-to: foco_eventos.rep_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="reconstruir"; !}

@rep_s_testigo
go-to: foco_eventos.rep_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p2="testigo"; !}

@rep_fin
new-page: true
face-image: img/countryside2.jpg
