Q.ej3_nodo="atoyac"; Q.ej3_f=44; Q.ej1_f=(Q.ej1_f||46)+14;
if(Q.apoyo_popular<0){Q.apoyo_popular=0;} if(Q.f_cerco>100){Q.f_cerco=100;}
!}

= El puño

[? if ch_p2 = "dinero" : The suitcases come up on a mule and they change what the column can do for two years — real rifles, real boots, medicine, a radio. They also come up with a headline. The papers run the family photograph and the mother on television, and the government, which has been burning villages in this state for four years without troubling a single front page, is abruptly the reasonable party in a story about men who take a boy for money. The PCM's people stop returning your messages. You have armed the revolution and rented out its name. ?][? if ch_p2 = "presos" : You ask for people instead of money and the state has to do the one thing it cannot do gracefully, which is admit it is holding them. Forty-one campesinos walk out of the state penitentiary. Nine names from the airbase are answered with an official silence that is itself the loudest testimony of the war. Four of the released walk straight up into the sierra and into your column, which the state's own lawyers will later cite as proof that the deal was a mistake — and they will be right, and it will still have been the correct thing to have asked for. ?][? if ch_p2 = "tierra" : You ask for the titles, and for a week the Republic of Mexico has to conduct, on the radio, an argument about whether one rich boy's life is worth a filing cabinet full of land his family stole in 1958. It concedes. It concedes on air. The papers are signed and read out and four ejidos exist again by the end of the month, and in every valley in the Costa Grande people who have never met you understand precisely what happened and who did it. It is the single most effective act of agrarian reform in Guerrero since Cárdenas, and it was carried out by twenty people with rifles and a hostage. ?]

And then the fist closes, exactly as it closed on Lucio.

Thousands of troops into a state that had hundreds. The airbase working around the clock. Every road in the Costa Grande with a checkpoint on it and every village with a list. Paratroopers on the ground at Atoyac by the end of the month. The sierra becomes the most heavily hunted piece of ground in the country and stays that way, and every single thing the column does from here on is done inside that fact.

You bought a great deal in one afternoon. Now you have to survive having bought it.

- @root: Continuar.

# =====================================================================
# EL ENLACE CON LA CIUDAD — the link, the protocol, and whether the thread gets pulled.
# =====================================================================
@ev_enlace
title: El enlace con la ciudad
new-page: true
face-image: img/countrysideravine.jpg
subtitle: A hand extended from the urban war
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and f_hombres >= 16 and time >= f_ev_last + 4 and f_enlace_foco = 0
priority: 4
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {! Q.f_enlace_foco=1; Q.f_ev_last=Q.time; Q.ch_p1=""; Q.ch_p2=""; Q.ch_res=""; !}

= El enlace con la ciudad

He arrives with the right password and city shoes, and he is visibly, comically unfit for the last four hours of the walk, and he has been carrying a proposal in his head rather than on paper, which is at least professional.

The urban comrades can move you things the sierra never will: clean weapons bought with expropriated money, false papers that survive a checkpoint, medicine in quantity, a route to the coast and out of the country for anyone who has to disappear. What they want in return is coordination — that when they act in the cities your war in the south moves too, so the state cannot concentrate on either of you. It is the synthesis Che preached and almost never achieved, the city and the mountain as a single war.

It is also a thread. Every link is a thread, and the DFS has spent six years getting extremely good at pulling threads.

- @enl_si: Take the link, fully. Two-way coordination, shared timing, everything. *(the most gained; the most exposed)*
- @enl_asimetrico: Take what they offer and give nothing back — no timings, no locations, no coordination. *(cynical; keeps you safer; they will eventually notice)*
- @enl_no: Send him back with thanks. The sierra can be betrayed by no one it has never met. *(nothing gained; nothing to pull)*

@enl_no
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! Q.ch_p1="no"; Q.f_moral+=2; Q.disciplina=(Q.disciplina||65)+2; !}

= Bajó al día siguiente

You feed him, let him sleep, and send him back down in the morning with thanks and nothing else, and he takes it well, which somehow makes it worse.

The city's war is better armed than yours and better educated than yours and it is being rolled up cell by cell in exactly the way a network can be and a mountain cannot. You keep your war small and slow and yours. It is a real choice with a real cost and you will spend the next two years being unable to buy antibiotics.

- @root: Continuar.

